The news goes back to 2000 but it speaks to your point on the removal of selective availability built into the GPS system. Then again, when our government gives us something it usually means they have something much, much, more advanced that they've created in a lab that 'doesn't exist.'  No worries, even if somebody managed to find out about it, the government would neither confirm nor deny its existence.


