		<outline text="Teenagers">
			<outline text=" Caroline 	

caroline@jedimaster.smith.edu &lt;mailto:caroline@jedimaster.smith.edu&gt; to adam
	 More options	  Aug 27 (2 days ago)
Ahoy Adam.
       In the DSC today you mentioned that you hadn't gotten any feedback
from teenagers... So here you go. I'm about the same age as Christina
(turning 15 in a couple months) and, speaking as a teenage girl (and
oldest child), I can tell you that fathers are no picnic either. Your
relationship with her actually reminds me a lot of mine with my dad
and, although I love him dearly, he's a hassle. My parents haven't
experienced a child grow up before, and it seems to be harder for them
to let go of me than for me to renounce them. Go figure.
       Also worth mentioning, I think, is that (in my case) much of the
insolence and rebellion is calculated. We teenagers are smarter than
you think. After 15 years of living under the rule of parents, we have
learned how to manipulate, placate, and annoy you in ways that I don't
think you understand. Or maybe my parents are just easy. Whatever the
reason, I think that us capable, intelligent teenage girls are vastly
underrated. I don't really know what Christina is like, but I would bet
that she has things much more under control than you believe.
       Thanks for your great podcast, if not for your love of teenagers. =)
- Caroline"/>
