			<outline text="buying music after hearing it">
				<outline text=" Brett Rann 	

brett@breesestreet.org &lt;mailto:brett@breesestreet.org&gt; to adam
	 More options	  Aug 27 (2 days ago)
I certainly go looking for it after I hear it on your show!


Unfortunately I'm in australia and we don't have much option for
buying music online -- i think there' s a couple but it's windows
media player drm stuff and we're a 100% mac house.  I'd much rather
pay $1-$2 than spend half an hour digging through the scum of p2p and
cleverly crafted google searches to find a song.


I'm currently looking for earth wind and fire fantasy... love that
song!  Found &quot;groove tonight&quot; here mp3.jet2web.net—data &lt;http://mp3.jet2web.net/data/&gt;

online_classics/dance_classics1/, which is ok, but I'd much rather
fantasy.  This is after about 15 minutes of searching.  Who knows how
much longer before I can find Fantasy.  Half an hour of my time is
worth much more than $1-2 freaking dollars.  C'est la vie!  At least
Apple is on the case.


A few friends use www.allofmp3.com &lt;http://www.allofmp3.com/&gt; which I think is some
russian site that offers music downloads for unbelievably low prices,
and apparently don't really pass on any royalties.  I'd rather get it
for free than give them some $  !


It's insane that the only way I can get my music easily is to either
order a CD online and wait a few days for delivery, or make a trip to
the city and cross my fingers that they have the album I'm after.


Keep that podsafe stuff coming through!


Brett
--
software developer in melbourne, australia."/>
